/**
 * ON THE CHART — how each product actually looks, on a real NinjaTrader 8
 * chart, with nothing added (Tom, 2026-09-21: "the product page is lacking how
 * the indicators look on chart, this should settle that once and for all").
 *
 * Source: "02 Product Masters\\0920 NEW Product Cover & Images\\Product Images\\
 * New Raw Images" — 34 screenshots, 3840x2160, all on NinjaTrader's own black
 * ground (#040404, sampled). Served at 2560x1440 (webp q88) as
 * `/charts/<slug>-<n>.webp`; the source file is noted beside each entry.
 * A re-exported picture gets a NEW filename (one-year immutable asset cache).
 *
 * 2026-10-01: DS Zones and DS Iceberg were redrawn (Build 2026-10-01). Their
 * pre-redesign stills (orange KEY LEVEL card, "ICE RES / ICE SUP" badges) were
 * replaced with Tom's new screenshots from "Master Product Folder\\DS Zones\\Media"
 * and "...\\DS Iceberg\\Media" — 1920x1080, served at their native size as
 * lossless webp (smaller than lossy here: the charts are mostly black), never
 * enlarged, as gex-1-v2 and the Session levels pair already are.
 *
 * 2026-10-05 — the pictures of DS Stochastics, DS Squeeze and DS ASL are the
 * same screenshots as before under new filenames (stochastics-*, squeeze-*,
 * asl-*). Each still shows its OLD name in the panel title or the chart's
 * indicator list, so they are Tom's to re-shoot. DS MACD has no picture here
 * yet. DS VWAP's two (DS Media\\02 Products\\DS VWAP, 2560x1440, lossless)
 * went in on 2026-10-06.
 *
 * 2026-10-06 — DS ProLiquidityHunter and DS ProHeikinAshi: Tom's raw
 * NinjaTrader screenshots (DS Media\\02 Products\\<name>, 2560x1440, served at
 * that size, lossless). The third of each is on his light chart template.
 * DS ProHeikinAshi's second and third were taken on the build before the
 * panel label was corrected and read "DS ProHeikenAshi" at the panel's top
 * left; the first is the current build.
 *
 * ORDER: the picture that shows the product most completely comes first (it
 * leads the page), then the others.
 *
 * CAPTIONS say what is ON the picture, read from its own labels ("ICE RES 9x",
 * "CROSS 28962.00", "QUAD OVERSOLD", "Call Wall"…) and the product's own copy —
 * no outcome, no forecast, no superlative (NinjaTrader vendor guidelines).
 * Where the picture proves nothing beyond "this is the product", the caption
 * says only that.
 *
 * DS Bulk Replay Downloader has none: it is a data utility with no chart of its
 * own, so its page leads with its product-guide boards as before.
 */
export type ChartShot = { src: string; caption: string; blur: string };

/** Every chart is 2560x1440 — one shape, so the stage never changes size. */
export const CHART_W = 2560;
export const CHART_H = 1440;
